>> title: Croissant
>> category: Pastry & Doughs
>> tags: pastry, laminated, breakfast, butter, oven
>> counters: Bakery
>> aka: croissant, croissants, butter croissant, croissant au beurre, plain croissant, crescent roll
>> pairs-with: croissant-dough, almond-croissant
>> servings: 12
>> time: 3 hr
>> slack: narrow — the proof is judged by a wobble: under-proofed they push their butter out into the pan, over-proofed they collapse as they bake
>> step.1: roll to a 8x24-in sheet
>> step.2: cut twelve triangles and roll each one up
>> step.3: proof 2 hr, until they wobble
>> step.4: beat the egg wash
>> step.5: brush and bake 400°F (205°C) 18 min

Roll @croissant dough{1%batch}(cold, one batch of croissant-dough) out on @all-purpose flour{2%Tbs}(for dusting) to a sheet 8 inches deep and 24 inches long, a scant quarter-inch thick.

Cut @&(~1)dough sheet{} into twelve long triangles with a 4-inch base, stretch each one out by its point, and roll it up from the base — three turns showing, point tucked underneath.

Proof @&(~1)shaped croissants{} on lined trays at room temperature for ~proof{2%hr}, until they have nearly doubled and wobble as one piece when the tray is shaken. Proof them warmer than this and the butter runs out onto the tray instead of steaming inside the layers.

Beat @egg{1%large} with @whole milk{1%Tbs}(15 mL) until it is loose enough to brush without dragging.

Brush @&(~2)proofed croissants{} with @&(~1)egg wash{} and bake in a 400°F (205°C) #oven{} for ~bake{18%min}, until they are deep brown at the ridges and sound hollow. Pale croissants are underbaked ones; the colour is the crust.
